            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-08T14:17:25.419649+00:00",
            "notes": "Add even more wall and maximize AP (I generally sell [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56) if I have a lot of cash and can throw on a higher AP / value epic)! Typical engagement cycle would be to wall off and isolate / catch a target in the blizzard, run at them and left click the hell out of them, pop Coulder when you're about to die (always pop sooner rather than later - game can have input lag issues), keep rolling into them, and pop another wall right behind them when Coulder ends and continue left clicking them. Unless you're running into a heavy cleanse comp like Zarya / Kiriko, target stands no chance.\n\nKey is to play around your cooldowns - don't engage unless you're confident you can disengage. With double walls and high CDR, you should still have plenty of uptime. You should now be able to destroy squishies with ease or farm a ton of ult from grouped up teams",
